      "problem": "$-12u+6(v+2u)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $6$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-12u+6(v+2u) & = \\\\ -12u+6\\cdot v+6\\cdot 2u & = \\\\ -12u+(6v)+(12u) & = \\\\ -12u+6v+12u & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-12u+6v+12u & = \\\\ (12u-12u)+6v & = \\\\ 6v\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
